  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array AAA of length NNN, with elements between 111 and NNN.\n\nYou will perform the following operation **exactly once**:\n\n\nChoose two indices LLL and RRR (1≤L≤R≤N1 \\leq L \\leq R \\leq N1≤L≤R≤N).\nThen, choose an integer XXX (1≤X≤N1 \\leq X \\leq N1≤X≤N) such that XXX **does not appear** among [AL,AL+1,AL+2,…,AR][A_L, A_{L+1}, A_{L+2}, \\ldots, A_R][AL​,AL+1​,AL+2​,…,AR​].\nFinally, for each iii from LLL to RRR (inclusive of both), set AiA_iAi​ to XXX.\nFor example, if A=[3,1,4,1,5]A = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5]A=[3,1,4,1,5], choosing L=2,R=4,X=2L = 2, R = 4, X = 2L=2,R=4,X=2 will result in the array [3,2,2,2,5][3, 2, 2, 2, 5][3,2,2,2,5].\n\nHow many of these operations will result in AAA being sorted in non-decreasing order?\n\nTwo operations are considered different if the tuples (L,R,X)(L, R, X)(L,R,X) determining them are different.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of operations that result in AAA being sorted in non-descending order.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3\\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤N1 \\leq A_i \\leq N1≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053\\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3\n1 1 3\n4\n4 3 2 1\n5\n2 4 2 4 2\n5\n3 1 4 1 5",
        "output": "8\n2\n7\n6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The 888 valid operations, represented by their tuples (L,R,X)(L, R, X)(L,R,X), are:\n\n(1,2,2)(1, 2, 2)(1,2,2)\n(1,2,3)(1, 2, 3)(1,2,3)\n(1,3,2)(1, 3, 2)(1,3,2)\n(2,2,2)(2, 2, 2)(2,2,2)\n(2,2,3)(2, 2, 3)(2,2,3)\n(2,3,2)(2, 3, 2)(2,3,2)\n(3,3,1)(3, 3, 1)(3,3,1)\n(3,3,2)(3, 3, 2)(3,3,2)\n\nThe tuple (1,1,2)(1, 1, 2)(1,1,2) is invalid for example, because with it we obtain A=[2,1,3]A = [2, 1, 3]A=[2,1,3] which is not sorted.\nTest case 222: The only valid operations are (1,3,1)(1, 3, 1)(1,3,1) and (2,4,4)(2, 4, 4)(2,4,4)."
      }
    ]
